\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18.4.1}{\ignorespaces Tree \(T\) with each node annotated \emph  {v}[\(\tin  (v),\tout  (v)\)] (Ch.~5's tour, \(\tout  \) inclusive). The orange strip is the Euler array: slot~\(p\) holds node \(\mathit  {euler}[p]\), read as \((1,2,4,5,8,3,6,7,9,10)\). The two shaded bars are the intervals a BIT is handed to answer ``sum/add subtree(2)'' and ``sum/add subtree(3)'' -- the whole tree collapses to contiguous slots. Node~3 sits at slot~6, so it is \emph  {outside} the subtree(2) bar even though it is drawn beside node~2 in the picture.}}{1115}{figure.caption.195}\protected@file@percent }
